I enter the office.
I sit in my chair.
I open my bag.
I take out the laptop.
I start the laptop.
I write code.
This code is very difficult.
Rohan comes over to me.
"Good morning, Maya," Rohan says.
"Good morning, Rohan," I say.
"Are you busy?" he asks.
"Yes, this code is difficult," I say.
Rohan looks at my laptop.
He helps.
We look at that code.
He points out an error there.
I quickly fix the code.
Now it is correct.
"Thank you, Rohan," I say.
He goes to his chair.
